        <lomm:title><lomm:string language="en">Introductory astronomy: gravity, starlight and other worlds</lomm:string></lomm:title>
        <lomm:language>en</lomm:language>
        <lomm:description><lomm:string language="en">Four units for a first course in astronomy, built from Gravitas investigations that are already published. Students watch the sky move and explain it, find what decides whether an orbit comes back, read a star's temperature and size from its light, and measure a real planet around another star. Each unit has an optional reading or model for students who want the background first, and an advanced investigation for students who want more.</lomm:string></lomm:description>
      </lomm:general>
      <lomm:rights>
        <lomm:description><lomm:string language="en">Each link opens Gravitas in a browser. Gravitas is MIT-licensed software and its teaching material is CC BY 4.0; readings and data keep the licences shown with them. Nothing about students is carried, and no grades come back.</lomm:string></lomm:description>
      </lomm:rights>
    </lomm:lom>
